# alt_takeoff_steer.expect — pilot attitude control DURING the ALT_HOLD auto-takeoff climb
# ALT_HOLD 自動離陸の上昇中のパイロット姿勢制御
#
# The roll stick goes RIGHT after a short (2.0 s) centred head start from ARM (event C0
# in the .scn — see the justification below).
# [9.8,10.6] is the TakeoffClimb window (altitude still climbing, ~0.20→0.39 m).
# The craft MUST tilt there (tilt_max > 6°) — proving attitude is never locked out during
# auto-takeoff (a level-attitude hold would give tilt ≈ 0). The auto-vertical still carries
# it to 0.5 m and reaches Airborne, then centering self-levels.
# ロールは ARM から 2.0 秒の中立頭出し(C0)の後に右へ。[9.8,10.6] は TakeoffClimb
# 窓（高度 約0.20→0.39 m 上昇中）。そこで機体は傾く必要（tilt_max > 6°）— 自動離陸中も
# 姿勢を奪わない証明（水平保持なら tilt≈0）。鉛直は自動で 0.5 m へ到達し Airborne、
# 中央復帰で水平化。
#
# All metric windows sit after C0 (the 2.0 s head start). At hover duty 0.7245, a roll
# disturbance right after ARM (climb=0) leaves too little auto-vertical margin: alt_mean keeps
# sinking short of the 0.5 m target even after centring (measured without the head start: [12.5,13.5] alt_mean=0.296).
# With the 2.0 s centred-stick head start the climb gets a run-up; the tilt amount
# and duty health are unchanged by it (tilt_max, duty_max), and after centring the craft recovers to 0.5 m and
# settles (measured: [14.5,15.5] alt_mean=0.588).
# 全メトリクス窓は C0(2.0s頭出し)の後ろに置く。ホバーduty=0.7245 では、ARM直後(climb=0)にロール
# 外乱を当てると自動垂直側の余裕が足りず、centre後もalt_mean が目標(0.5m)未達のまま
# 沈下し続ける(頭出しなしの実測: [12.5,13.5] alt_mean=0.296)。2.0s
# centered stick の頭出し(C0)で上昇に助走を付けると、傾き量
# ・duty健全性は頭出しで変わらず(tilt_max・duty_max)、centre後は0.5mへ回復・整定する
# (実測: [14.5,15.5] alt_mean=0.588)。
exit 0
log_contains any "Auto-takeoff complete — normal mode law engaged"
# Roll RESPONDS during the takeoff climb (the key behaviour — a level hold would give tilt ≈ 0).
metric tilt_max > 0.1047  in 9.8 10.6  # 6.0 deg
metric tilt_max < 0.4363 in 9.5 12.6  # 25.0 deg
# Auto-vertical recovers to hold ~0.5 m after self-leveling (D's settled tail).
metric alt_mean > 0.42 in 14.5 15.5
metric alt_mean < 0.70 in 14.5 15.5
metric duty_max < 0.95 in 9.5 15.0
